    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0342" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.61/995: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-09T14:00:00+03:00">February 9, 1943—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 10—12:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. The Polish Chargé d’Affaires<anchor n="34" xml:id="d243-f1"/> informed me
                    yesterday that there has been no change or improvement in Polish-Soviet
                        relations.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d243-f2"/> He stated somewhat resignedly
                    that the Soviet Government was still adamant in respect to the release of Polish
                    officers, the evacuation of <pb facs="0343" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/> Polish
                    women and children and its policy toward Polish Jews. He said that Polish
                    citizens are now being conscripted into the Red Army in spite of the protests of
                    the Polish Embassy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="34" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p>Henryk Sokolnicki.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d243-f2" n="35" xml:id="d243-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram Polish Series No. 3, January 28, midnight, from the Ambassador to
                    the Polish Government in Exile, and footnote 20, <ref target="#pg323">p.
                        323</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
